{% set fw = bcv2Firmware.product %}
<article class="note-page bcv2-update" data-updater data-firmware-url="{{ fw.download | replace('https://anasmalas.com', '') }}" data-firmware-sha256="{{ fw.sha256 }}" data-firmware-version="{{ fw.latest }}">
  <header class="note-hero shell reading-width">
    <a class="back-link" href="/bcv2/">← BCv2 guide</a>
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>BCv2</p>
    <h1 class="note-title">Update your card</h1>
    <p class="note-dek">The latest firmware is {% if fw.name %}{{ fw.name }} ({{ fw.latest }}){% else %}{{ fw.latest }}{% endif %}, from {{ fw.date | readableDate }}. <a href="/bcv2/changelog/">Whats new</a></p>
    <p class="update-warning" data-usb-warning hidden>Firefox, Safari and every browser on iPhone and iPad don't support WebUSB. Use Chrome or Edge to update here.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="note-body reading-width">
    <section class="update-card" data-route="browser" hidden>
      <h2>Update now <span class="beta" data-beta>Beta</span></h2>
      <ol class="update-steps">
        <li>With the card fully disconnected, plug the DATA port into this <span data-device>computer</span>.</li>
        <li>Hold the BOOT button then plug a power supply into the POWER port. A moment after the card is plugged in, let go of BOOT. The card is in bootloader mode for the next 20 seconds or so, try again if the lights come on before you can update it.</li>
        <li>Press Update, select "Unknown device from QinHeng Electronics (WCH)", and allow your browser to connect to it. You will see the update status on this page.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="update-aside" data-linux-help hidden>First time on Linux? Chrome needs a udev rule, its under <a href="#trouble" data-open-trouble>Trouble</a>.</p>
      <button class="update-button" type="button" data-update>Update</button>
      <div class="update-progress" data-progress hidden>
        <progress max="100" value="0"></progress>
        <p><span data-status>Getting the firmware…</span> Keep the card plugged in.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="update-result" data-result role="status" hidden></p>
      <p class="update-aside update-hint">You can use a phone with USB C to power the card, and another to update it.</p>
      <div class="update-fallback" data-windows-help hidden>
        <button class="update-link" type="button" data-more-ways aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="more-ways">Didn't work? More methods</button>
