          <div class="update-method">
            <h3>Install the driver</h3>
            <p>The browser needs the WinUSB driver for the card's bootloader. You only do this once:</p>
            <ol>
              <li>Put the card in bootloader mode (step 2) and open <a href="https://zadig.akeo.ie" rel="noopener">Zadig</a>.</li>
              <li>Pick the device whose USB ID reads 4348 55E0 (or 1A86 55E0). It may be called "USB Module" or "Unknown Device". Not listed? Options &gt; List All Devices.</li>
              <li>Leave the driver on WinUSB and click Install Driver (or Replace Driver).</li>
              <li>Put the card back in bootloader mode and press Update again.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>Only change that one device. If you used WCHISPTool, it will need its own driver back.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="update-method">
            <h3>Download the flash script <span class="beta">Beta</span></h3>
            <p>Get the <a href="/bcv2/flash/bcv2-flasher.ps1" download>Windows flasher</a>, right click it and pick "Run with PowerShell" (on Windows 11 it might be under "Show more options"). It walks you through the driver the first time, then flashes every card you plug in.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
