    <details class="update-more">
      <summary>Is it safe?</summary>
      <p>The card's bootloader lives in its own memory that an update cant touch, so if anything goes wrong just put it back in bootloader mode and try again.</p>
      <p>The browser can only talk to the card you pick in the list. The firmware is checked against its SHA-256 before it gets written.</p>
      <p>The easy flashers are short plain scripts, read them or ask your friendly LLM to review. They only download <a href="https://github.com/ch32-rs/wchisp" rel="noopener">wchisp</a> v0.3.0 from its GitHub page and the firmware from this site, and check both against fixed SHA-256 hashes. No admin needed, except the Linux udev rule, and on Windows the Microsoft C++ runtime and the driver if you dont have them yet.</p>
      <p>All of it is <a href="https://github.com/AnasMalas/AnasMalas.github.io/tree/main/src/bcv2/flash" rel="noopener">on GitHub</a>.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="update-more" id="trouble" data-trouble>
      <summary>Trouble?</summary>
      <p><strong>Card not in the list, or the display came on?</strong> It didnt go into the bootloader. Unplug POWER, hold BOOT a bit harder and plug it back in.</p>
      <p><strong>Windows:</strong> the browser needs a driver for the card. Run the Windows flasher once and it sets it up with Zadig, or just use your phone.</p>
      <p><strong>Linux:</strong> Chrome needs a udev rule to use the card. Run this once, then unplug POWER and plug it back in with BOOT held:</p>
      <pre><code>sudo tee /etc/udev/rules.d/60-bcv2-wchisp.rules &lt;&lt;'EOF'
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="4348", ATTRS{idProduct}=="55e0", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="55e0", TAG+="uaccess"
EOF
sudo udevadm control --reload-rules &amp;&amp; sudo udevadm trigger</code></pre>
      <p><strong>Stopped partway?</strong> Nothing is broken. Put it back in bootloader mode and update again.</p>
    </details>

    <p class="update-follow">To get an email for new firmware, watch the <a href="{{ bcv2Releases.repo }}" rel="noopener">BCv2 releases</a> on GitHub (Watch &gt; Custom &gt; Releases), or use the <a href="{{ bcv2Releases.feed }}">feed</a>.</p>
